  <h2>Where AI helps in construction management</h2>
  <p>Construction managers benefit most from AI on <strong>schedule and document drafting</strong>, <strong>safety Q&amp;A and reporting</strong>, and <strong>subcontractor coordination</strong>. AI is not a substitute for the CM's judgement, the OSHA-required safety program, or the project schedule of record (P6, MS Project, Procore). Used at the front of the workflow, however, it removes the most repetitive drafting hours from the superintendent and the project engineer.</p>

  <p><em>Official references:</em> <a href="https://www.osha.gov/construction" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">OSHA Construction Standards</a> · <a href="https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-10/documents/swppp_designer_brief.pdf" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">EPA SWPPP Designer Brief</a> · <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/construction/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">NIOSH Construction Safety</a></p>

